  "receiptMarkdown": "# Receipt \u2014 pri-c015-aso-protected-proof\n\nStatus: **review candidate**\n\n## Qualified capability\n\nThe selected browser PGlite `shape-only` topology passed current-source\nprotected replication from Gate and FRF shapes through transactional SQL\nmaterialization into the PEM graph. The candidate establishes one authoritative\nclinical shape writer, atomic row/checkpoint recovery, authorized graph\nrecovery, practice and logout fencing, interrupted-body recovery, projection\nand local-only-field egress, handle expiry/refetch, stream revocation and\nclient/backend isolation.\n\n## Source identity\n\n| Repository | HEAD | Selected-source aggregate | Files |\n|---|---|---|---:|\n| ASO | `d95242542060d1e19a6efe9143f57c015d6162f4` | `8c8c60eb49bb56e37aab78c0e2f09a3b17470a47d6381c039f5c00866f501ecd` | 97 |\n| FABRIC | `ae26f45d8afa037677004cd118b0571b8b552131` | `60e5ec0775a0b0e96911fa9868e97d6b2e9ae1028288ae5f9303aa2f73976f43` | 384 |\n| GATE | `77914a2ad2e3cd57f12fd9131fa8cdddf625f68e` | `95d7b46655809d6aeade146365e44a26c4192144c7658f2d9b07f72b23974315` | 79 |\n\nThe final source manifest matches the authoritative campaign for all three\nrepositories and records every selected file, dirty-state hashes, contract\nfiles, runtime image IDs and OCI source labels.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Authoritative protected campaign: passed.\n- ASO focused tests: 99 passed.\n- Fabric current revocation suite: 4 passed.\n- Retained Fabric revocation and lease-timing suite: 10 passed, maximum 1,500 ms\n  against the accepted 5,000 ms bound.\n- Mounted durability and ownership checks: 13 passed.\n- Mounted Chrome lifecycle checks: 9 passed across two practices.\n- Browser interruption and recovery checks: 10 passed.\n- Protected composition checks: 10 passed.\n- Network topology checks: 9 passed.\n- ASO Python compilation, typecheck, lint, production build and architecture\n  audit: passed.\n- Fabric `cargo check -p frf-app -p frf-gateway`: passed.\n- Gate replica-grant tests: passed.\n- Strict OpenSpec validation: passed.\n\nThe ASO build retained upstream PGlite/Rollup warnings about browser-external\nNode filesystem symbols, dependency `eval`, and the existing large main chunk.\n\nThe browser run's c014-owned RSS metric exceeded 512 MiB and is disclosed in\n`acceptance-b.md` and `receipt.json`; it does not alter c015's passed functional\nacceptance.\n\n## Primary evidence\n\n- `receipt.json`: `8b8675076ff34177668f2003afe89a7f825934b94ac3f5b5e5d93fbd2bcdd476`\n- `source-manifest.json`: `540d1cf82b10d4dfc7360b2f0f19f046343d7a6276f8bcec96d7ab98df2428e6`\n- `quality-checks.json`: `5374c3d61a452671ad84594a808818c9a63cb9fb4845613391c97b16f4e0d786`\n- `campaign.json`: `6abf86af9336ece7e2fd32a6229f85d039e9b43b4cc20ff0415aa00cb00bea51`\n- `acceptance-a.md`: `a1a42d5f6cd6484c2376e774b7d0f27d6fe639b7ec7d72848e7cb679ae64e70e`\n- `acceptance-b.md`: `abc9b7aa865472e5ea1552cc685526b6824a3642a67ec88f8065e3dcf4a733ff`\n\n`receipt.json` inventories 15 primary artifacts by size and\nSHA-256. Failed and diagnostic attempts remain explicit historical evidence and\nare excluded from the passing claim.\n",
  "acceptanceA": "# Acceptance A \u2014 transactional recovery and session fencing\n\nResult: **Passed**\n\n## Crash and recovery\n\nThe current-source mounted materializer passed all thirteen durability and\nownership checks on the 16,203-row protected dataset. It proved that an\ninterruption before commit leaves neither partial rows nor a checkpoint, a\nfailure during materialization rolls back the row and checkpoint together, and\na restart after SQL commit but before PEM publication reconstructs the graph\nfrom durable authorized state without skipping the committed revision.\n\nDisposed owners could not publish a pending revision. The replacement owner\napplied that revision coherently to SQL and PEM, and authority loss emitted a\nrevalidation failure while retaining the last authorized SQL, checkpoint and\ngraph state.\n\n## Mounted logout and practice switch\n\nThe shipping `SessionProvider` and `GraphProvider` were mounted in Chrome with\ntwo independent Kratos sessions and two populated practices. Both graphs\ncontained the expected seven projections. Practice switch and logout removed\nthe protected view synchronously, the old graph was absent before replacement,\nno successful old-scope response completed after either fence, and the\nreplacement session was revoked through the real Kratos admin endpoint. Its\nsubsequent Gate request returned HTTP 401.\n\nAll synthetic identities, relational rows, PGlite state, helper state and\nservice changes were removed or restored by the campaign cleanup.\n\n## Source-bound evidence\n\n| Artifact | SHA-256 |\n|---|---|\n| `campaign.json` | `6abf86af9336ece7e2fd32a6229f85d039e9b43b4cc20ff0415aa00cb00bea51` |\n| `task-4-mounted-materializer.json` | `3295c7d983f9f16e8f78dc4e04500c0371c2758ded8729c3184423926ee69f93` |\n| `task-4-mounted-browser-memory.json` | `9b08419b97cb587f9ad42a26e86dc18d0e390a3d9b8551a8a1683ef9103ab532` |\n\nThe campaign reports unchanged selected source for ASO, Fabric and Gate between\nits before and after snapshots.\n",
  "acceptanceB": "# Acceptance B \u2014 interruption, authorization and egress boundaries\n\nResult: **Passed** for the selected browser PGlite `shape-only` topology.\n\n## Interrupted bodies and egress\n\nA real Chrome request received HTTP 200 and the first 256 bytes of a live Gate\nshape response, then a browser `ReadableStream` error interrupted JSON parsing.\nThe mounted transport rejected the response without publishing SQL rows, a\ncheckpoint or PEM entities. Its next request was cold and hydrated the complete\nauthorized dataset.\n\nThe focused 99-test suite also projected an over-wide clinical row onto the\napproved SQL target. Forbidden `member_id` and local-only `local_embedding`\ncanaries did not reach the generated statement.\n\n## Authorization, expiry and revocation\n\nThe live composition passed ten checks: initial authorization, same-session\ncontinuation, authenticated cross-identity handle denial, practice-scope\ndenial, projection denial, per-request grant revalidation, handle expiry to\nHTTP 409 without shape headers, and authorized cold refetch with a fresh\nhandle/offset.\n\nCurrent-source Fabric revocation tests passed 4/4 in the authoritative campaign.\nThe retained lease-timing receipt passed 10/10 with a 1,500 ms maximum against\nthe accepted 5,000 ms bound. Mounted logout independently revoked the live\nKratos session and the next protected request returned HTTP 401.\n\n## Network and writer isolation\n\nGate is the only host-reachable protected shape endpoint. Electric and the FRF\nfacade expose zero host ports and occupy only the backend network. The client\nsegment reached Gate and received a session challenge but could not resolve or\nreach FRF, Electric or the operator diagnostic. A host-browser-position probe\nalso could not reach Electric directly.\n\nThe 34-file production provider closure wires the FRF shape transport to the SQL\nmaterializer and contains no generic entity-watch writer symbol. Runtime request\ntracing observed shape requests only.\n\n## File-size boundary\n\nEvery c015-modified ASO file is at most 500 lines. The campaign coordinator is\n497 lines and the browser runner is 428 lines. Pre-existing oversized files that\nwere not modified by c015 remain tracked separately.\n\nThe current browser run recorded 591,396,864 bytes of renderer RSS growth,\nabove c014's 512 MiB memory threshold. It is retained as a nonblocking\nobservation here because c014 owns and already archived the memory acceptance\ngate; all c015 functional, isolation and lifecycle checks passed.\n\n## Source-bound evidence\n\n| Artifact | SHA-256 |\n|---|---|\n| `campaign.json` | `6abf86af9336ece7e2fd32a6229f85d039e9b43b4cc20ff0415aa00cb00bea51` |\n| `protected-composition.json` | `81d29178369fcffb8941e49744a05a9b1cad218df632ffc74e08c03cde7f1559` |\n| `protected-topology.json` | `25f93143c2567423d8c73f6a6f9ae781f31a1122a7adc3779ce7506d40262563` |\n| `task-4-revocation-timing.json` | `2074b485c4c5f213886a2cd0f8991ca928524ddcd532203f79e814f3c52c4ccc` |\n| `task-4-mounted-browser-memory.json` | `9b08419b97cb587f9ad42a26e86dc18d0e390a3d9b8551a8a1683ef9103ab532` |\n",
  "semver": "# PRI c015 semver and rollout record\n\n## Public contract change\n\n`frf-ports` changes the public `ASO_PROJECTION_REVISION` constant from 3 to 4.\n`VerifiedClaims::aso_replica_scope` performs an exact revision match, so a\nrevision-3 ASO replica grant is rejected after Fabric adopts revision 4. The\nrevision advances because ASO's server-owned registry now grants seven exact\nprojections, including `annotation_types` and `annotations`, and expands the\napproved `cases` projection.\n\n## Semver classification\n\nThe workspace is currently `0.1.0`. This is a behaviorally breaking public-port\nchange for a pre-1.0 crate and requires the next pre-1.0 minor release rather\nthan a patch release. The release-signoff change must carry the resulting\nworkspace version and migration note; c015 does not publish packages.\n\n## Forward rollout\n\nASO, Flint Gate, and Fabric use one distributed exact-match contract:\n\n1. Build Gate and Fabric from source that declares revision 4.\n2. Replace both runtime images in the same maintenance window.\n3. Drain or revoke revision-3 grants and handles, then issue fresh revision-4\n   grants from ASO.\n4. Keep the protected browser profile unavailable until both images report\n   healthy and a revision-4 request passes through Gate to Fabric.\n\nMixed Gate/Fabric revisions fail closed with HTTP 403. No revision downgrade or\ncompatibility alias is provided because accepting both revisions would let an\nolder projection contract outlive its privacy review.\n\n## Rollback\n\nRollback is coordinated across ASO's projection registry, Gate's minted claim,\nFabric's exact-match constant, and the shape catalog. Stop new grants, drain\nrevision-4 handles, restore the prior four artifacts together, and issue new\nrevision-3 grants only after the prior catalog is active. Rolling back one\nparticipant alone intentionally leaves the protected path unavailable.\n",
